<title>THAILAND: Thai mills sees 1997 corn import of 400,000T.</title>
<headline>Thai mills sees 1997 corn import of 400,000T.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's animal feed industry on Monday projected it would import up to 400,000 tonnes of corn for 1997 against below 300,000 tonnes imported in 1996.</p>
<p>Soymeal imports were likely to reach one million tonnes, Prasit Damrongchietanon, president of the Thai Feed Mill Association told Reuters</p>
<p>He said the projection was based on a scenario that the prices of broken rice and tapioca, traditional substitutes of corn for animal feed ingredients, would be lower compared to last year's level.</p>
</text>
